short_label: III.6
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two circles touch one another, then they do not have the same center.
----
proof:

Let the two circles *ABC* and *CDE* touch one another at the point *C.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="230" height="230" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="III.6 diagram" src="propIII6.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "III.6",
        pivot: "F",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;90,190",
            "B;point;free;200,120",
            "C;point;free;60,60",
            "ABC;circle;circumcircle;A,B,C;0;0;black;random",
            "F;point;center;ABC;black;green",
            "D;point;free;90,160",
            "FB;line;connect;F,B",
            "FC;line;connect;F,C",
            "M;point;midpoint;C,D;0;0",
            "MN;line;perpendicular;M,C;0;0;0",
            "F';point;intersection;MN,FC;0;0",
            "CDE;circle;radius;F',C;0;0;black;random",
            "EE';line;chord;FB,CDE;0;0;0",
            "E;point;first;EE'"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

I say that they do not have the same center.

For, if possible, let it be *F.*  Join *FC,* and draw *FEB* through at random.

Then, since the point *F* is the center of the circle *ABC, FC* equals *FB.*  Again, since the point *F* is the center of the circle *CDE, FC* equals *FE.* [!just I.Def.15]

But *FC* was proved equal to *FB,* therefore *FE* also equals *FB,* the less equals the greater, which is impossible.

Therefore *F* is not the center of the circles *ABC* and *CDE.*

Therefore *if two circles touch one another, then they do not have the same center.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
<br clear=all>
----
guide:

As mentioned before, this proposition is almost the same as the previous.  Both could be included in one statement: circles that meet don't have the same center, or the contrapositive: concentric circles don't meet.

This proposition is not used in the rest of the *Elements.*
